menu "Example Configuration"

config EXAMPLE_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default "myssid"

config EXAMPLE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default "mypassword"

config EXAMPLE_SIMPLEOTA_TOKEN
    string "SimpleOTA project token"
    default "paste-your-project-token"
    help
        Create a project at https://simpleota.com, then copy a project API
        token with the device scope (Project -> API tokens).

choice EXAMPLE_SECURITY_MODE
    prompt "Security mode"
    default EXAMPLE_SECURITY_SIGNED
    help
        Signed: every update must carry a valid image signature from a
        pinned key. Strict signing: it must also carry a strict signature,
        which ties the image to this project and its build number. Strict
        signing needs the project id below and builds the SimpleOTA CLI has
        made strict-ready.

config EXAMPLE_SECURITY_SIGNED
    bool "Signed"

config EXAMPLE_SECURITY_STRICT
    bool "Strict signing"

endchoice

config EXAMPLE_SIMPLEOTA_PROJECT_ID
    string "SimpleOTA project id"
    default ""
    help
        The project's UUID, lowercase with hyphens, as the SimpleOTA CLI's
        key snippet prints it. Strict signing needs it. With Signed, setting
        it makes the device check a strict signature whenever an update
        carries one. Empty: strict signatures are not checked.

endmenu
